  <front>
    <title>IPv4 Service Continuity Prefix</title>
    <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="7335" stream="IETF"/>
    <date year="2014" month="August"/>
    <abstract pn="section-abstract">
      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">Dual-Stack Lite (DS-Lite), defined in RFC 6333, directs IANA to
reserve 192.0.0.0/29 for the Basic Bridging BroadBand (B4) element.
Per this memo, IANA has generalized that reservation to include other
cases where a non-routed IPv4 interface must be numbered as part of
an IPv6 transition solution.</t>
    </abstract>
